    },
    "message": "Check only the last tick's history records in per-tick validation\n\nThe engine validates the world after every tick without event history,\nbut the simulator extensions ignored that flag: every minute they\nre-parsed the whole shared-operations history (re-serializing each\nlinked event), the life-state social history and the resource-service\nrequest and stall histories. The cost grew with Run length, so a\n100-person Run slowed down by about 100 seconds per simulated day.\n\nPer-tick validation now checks the records appended during the tick\nthat just ended, plus the record before them for ordering. The care\nlifecycle replay and whole-history checks stay in the full validation\nat Run start and end and at Checkpoint capture and restore. Appended\nreceipts are already checked against their events when recorded.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UATazG2GqTVweGMJTJEbNT",
    "parents": [
